Is it accessible over the network?  i.e. can you ssh in a little while
after this point?

I had a problem with the same symptoms a while ago.. must have been
OpenBSD 3.2 or so.  In my case, /etc/ttys was not connecting the console
to the right place (i.e. doesn't pay attention to the SRM console
variable).  So after the initial boot, you don't see what's being copied
to /dev/console, and it looks "hung."

It sounds like you have console=graphics with some sort of VGA
and a PS/2 keyboard, so if you can ssh into the machine, look at /etc/ttys
and see what console is set to.

I don't have an Alpha with OpenBSD on it right now (gasp!) and I don't
use VGA/keyboard, so I'm not sure what it's supposed to look like.

